claimed: intent-vector-tier — the last tier, and the one the symbolic result makes interesting rather than redundant: BM25 plateaued at 60-64% agreement because it matches WORDS, and paraphrase is exactly where it is structurally weak. Class centroids over embeddings from the live gateway, then the same three numbers on the same split -- coverage at a margin, agreement with gold, and cost per message. The prediction to check rather than assume: if representation is the binding constraint the agreement curve should RISE with the margin where BM25 flat-lined; if it plateaus too, the honest conclusion is that the cheap-tier idea does not work on this taxonomy at all and both articles recommending it are wrong for this case. Embeddings are 1024-dim from the gateway, so a centroid is 4KB per class and scoring is a handful of dot products.
